<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- SpotBugs project decisions: a rule, or a rule in part of the code, that the team has decided not
     to enforce. One Match per decision, with a comment giving the reason, for example:

       <!- - JPA entities share associations by design (reason ...) - ->
       <Match><Package name="~team\.projectpulse\..*"/><Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP"/></Match>

     Unlike the baseline, this file may grow, but every entry is a reviewed decision. -->
<FindBugsFilter>
    <!-- EI_EXPOSE_REP / EI_EXPOSE_REP2 turned off project-wide. Project Pulse's mutable shared
         objects are of two kinds, and for both, sharing the reference is the design:
         1. JPA entities. Hibernate tracks changes through the live collection instance the entity
            holds, and 16 production call sites change entity collections through their getters
            (e.g. TeamService.transferTeam, UseCaseService). Returning copies would make those
            changes silently not persist, and 9 of the collections use orphanRemoval, where
            replacing the instance breaks Hibernate.
         2. Spring singletons injected through constructors, which the container shares by design. -->
    <Match><Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP,EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/></Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
